      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Bezoars are relatively common foreign body lesions of the stomach and intestine. Small bezoars can be treated using non-surgical methods, but large bezoars usually require open surgery. Occasionally they are giant-sized and may mimic an intra-abdominal mass clinically. We present the case of a 24-year-old woman with a giant gastric trichobezoar treated by open surgery; treatment methods are discussed."},
